From: Somraj Mani <somraj.mani@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 14:24:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] [BOLT][ARM] Support long-branch veneers

ARM B/BL reach +/-32MB and Thumb-2 BL +/-16MB, so rewritten layouts need
veneers far more often than on AArch64. Extend LongJmp to emit ARM and
Thumb long branches (absolute MOVW/MOVT + BX, which needs a fixed load
address), selecting the builder for the function being processed, and
extend VeneerElimination to recognise and remove linker-inserted ARM
veneers.

When a veneer redirects a call across the ARM/Thumb boundary, the call
instruction is rebuilt as BL or BLX to match the target's instruction
set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tdyp9Tb7sLvWDoCC5m4ACC
